# A user procedure called with a DIFFERENT case than its definition still raises
# `ol-not-enough-inputs`, and `params.callable` is the DEFINITION's declared spelling (`Double`),
# never the call site's casing (`DOUBLE`) nor a lowercasing — OpenLogo identifiers are
# case-insensitive, so the call spelling can never be the diagnostic's identity, and a MIXED-case
# declaration is what pins "declared spelling" apart from "lowercased call site"
# (spec/error-model.md:255-260; issue #1005, matching the check-side arity-procedure-declared-spelling
# fixture of issue #874).
define Double :a :b
  return :a + :b
end
print (DOUBLE 5)
